<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andaman and Nicobar Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Andaman and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicobar-islands">Nicobar Islands</a> are an archipelago in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>, a union territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> with its capital at Port Blair. The British established a penal colony there after 1857, later including the Cellular Jail. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> occupied the islands from 1942 to 1945 and handed nominal authority to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subhas-chandra-bose">Subhas Chandra Bose</a>'s Azad Hind government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andaman-and-nicobar-islands.jpg" alt="Andaman and Nicobar Islands" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ritiks · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Coral_Reef_at_the_Andaman_Islands.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
